Bulgarian spelling dictionary (bg_BG)

Source:   bgOffice project — https://bgoffice.sourceforge.net/
Packaged: LibreOffice/dictionaries, bg_BG

LICENCE — tri-licensed, and this application relies on the MPL branch.

The upstream project states, at https://bgoffice.sourceforge.net/ :

    "Лицензите, под които се разпространяват пакетите са GPLv2 или по-нова,
     LGPLv2 или по-нова и MPLv1.1."

    ("The licences under which the packages are distributed are GPLv2 or later,
      LGPLv2 or later, and MPLv1.1.")

Switcher3way relies on the **MPL-1.1** branch, which places this dictionary on exactly
the same footing as the bundled Ukrainian one, and keeps the MIT application code
unaffected — the dictionary is aggregated data, not linked code.

Note for whoever checks this next: the COPYING file shipped alongside the dictionary in
LibreOffice/dictionaries contains only the GPL v2 text, which understates the terms. It is
retained here as bg-COPYING-gpl2.txt. The tri-licence is stated by the upstream project,
not by that file — which is why the statement is quoted above rather than merely cited.
